  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The path to autonomy: socioeconomic empowerment of disabled women in Niamey via vocation and digital entrepreneurship training.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project specifically aims to strengthen the skills of women with disabilities in Niamey on digital technology, women&apos;s entrepreneurship and sewing, thus promoting their socio-economic inclusion.
To achieve these objectives, various activities are planned.
Firstly, the organisation of a kick-off workshop followed by two specific training sessions on the rights of persons with disabilities to raise awareness and prepare the participants for the continuation of the project (Activity 1).This will be followed by eight in-depth training sessions on entrepreneurship, digital marketing and the use of smartphones, providing beneficiaries with new skills (Activity 2). At the same time, 27 practical training sessions in women&apos;s sewing will be organized followed by the provision of sewing machines to strengthen their professional skills (Activity 3).
In addition, ten networking and networking sessions with institutions will be organised to open up new opportunities for beneficiaries (Activity 4). Finally, the organisation of the fair for women entrepreneurs with disabilities will promote and strengthen the visibility of their activities (Activity 5).
The expected outputs will be: 30 women with disabilities trained in their rights, digital technology and entrepreneurship; and know how to use social networks; 30 others trained in sewing and the provision of sewing machines to their groups (10 groups). These products will contribute directly to the achievement of the project&apos;s objectives, enabling the empowerment, promotion of activities and socio-economic inclusion of beneficiaries.</narrative>
  </description>
